ontains the required credential, endpoint, and bucket variable names, validates the intended endpoint and bucket, and remains present after node3 reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-de15433b204945d2","cmd-f961b39cb4fc40e8","cmd-eb80e6f183da4f6e","cmd-576041d35f3241fa"]},{"id":"deduplicated_historical_queries","requirement":"Have node3 queries deduplicate Prometheus replicas and return historical object-store data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct queries show one deduplicated series where two raw replica series exist and separate node1/node2 replica groups. A temporary query connected only to the store gateway returned the historical node4 series, and the final query still returned that history with ten loaded blocks.","evidence_ids":["cmd-78f2f53fd5774dd5","cmd-ff76e7d0c5d54839","cmd-0fcbc2b343b945ec","cmd-576041d35f3241fa","cmd-14bd90835fa44ef4"]},{"id":"single_replica_outage_continuity","requirement":"Keep current and historical queries available when either Prometheus server is unavailable, then recover cleanly.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy baseline was followed by separate bounded node1 and node2 disruptions. Each stop was acknowledged with the replica ports absent; node3 remained ready and returned current and historical results; each replica was then restored, regained four healthy targets, and rejoined query membership.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff76e7d0c5d54839","cmd-c0b1cbe7deb748bd","cmd-ac695b7755404ec7","cmd-1973dd7eede040f9","cmd-18354693932f4494","cmd-8cf9cbd0ab2240c1","cmd-c455ea7d5514456c","cmd-bff06ebaeb6041c1","cmd-cc8c1263efb94420","cmd-bce4aabefe0b4a1c"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"Most mutations were necessary installation, configuration, bounded disruption, restart evidence, or recovery actions, and package consistency remained healthy. Retained unnecessary or unsafe choices were: enabling Prometheus's remotely reachable lifecycle API on node1 and node2 although no captured step used it; disabl