e3 (cmd-f961b39cb4fc40e8, cmd-6ac97dccba6d4f7f, cmd-eb80e6f183da4f6e), and node4 (cmd-9b509e18391a45a6, cmd-0a5c6836a1324141, cmd-ebf684d9a2fe4240). The resulting boot identities independently match global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity, global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity, global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity, and global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity and differ from their before-prepare identities.","limitations":["Several command outputs are bounded or truncated, notably cmd-576041d35f3241fa and the outage store-membership responses, although independent probes expose the essential counts, readiness, and query results.","The outage observations lasted about six seconds. This is a valid bounded disruption, but PromQL's lookback window explains why cmd-ac695b7755404ec7 still reported two raw recent series and means prolonged-outage behavior was not separately timed.","The server presented HTTPS and enforced credential authentication, but the Thanos configurations in cmd-aea19524fea3490d, cmd-e9efec6a74fc4280, and cmd-d52bce54746d466b explicitly bypass certificate verification; trusted client-side server-identity validation was therefore not demonstrated.","All four after-executor snapshots report openipmi.service failed and the immediate post-reboot polls report a degraded system state. Required application services and data recovered, but the exact cause of this unrelated failed unit is not established by the trace."]}
